
<!-- SPLASH INTRO -->
<div class="splash-overlay" id="splashOverlay">
  {#
    muted is not optional here. Chrome refuses to autoplay a video with sound on
    a domain the visitor has no media engagement with, and when it refuses it
    also defers the resource load. The file then never downloads, no frame is
    ever decoded, and the overlay sits black until the fallback timer clears it.
    That is what the GitHub Pages site was doing on 6 Aug 2026: readyState 0 and
    networkState 2 fifteen seconds in. Muted autoplay is always permitted, so
    the video loads and plays, and the visitor can click for sound.
  #}
  <video id="splashVideo" playsinline autoplay muted preload="auto">
    <source src="/assets/video/Natural Trace Intro Cropped.mp4" type="video/mp4">
  </video>
  <div id="splashUnmute" style="position:absolute;bottom:2rem;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);font-size:.8rem;font-family:Montserrat,sans-serif;cursor:pointer;display:none">Click anywhere for sound</div>
  <div class="splash-skip" id="splashSkip">Skip</div>
</div>

<!-- NAV -->